            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0043" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">579.6AE1/40: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-02-01T17:00:00+00:00">February 1, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 1—1:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>137. Department’s 78, January 30, 6 p.m. Foreign Office advises orally that it
                    will notify interested governments at once of the additional items which the
                    United States wishes to add to the agenda.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
